{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-75317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $R=[3,4]\\times [5,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=4{x}^{2}+7{y}^{2}-12.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-75317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=4{x}^{2}+7{y}^{2}-12$ increases as $x$ increases on $[3,4],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y)=4{x}^{2}+7{y}^{2}-12$ increases as $y$ increases on $[5,6].$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=4{x}_{i-1}^{2}+7{y}_{j-1}^{2}-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(4{x}_{i-1}^{2}+7{y}_{j-1}^{2}-12)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $4{x}_{i-1}^{2}+7{y}_{j-1}^{2}-12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-75317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813289935f314fed96cd4ff74649733f6e26ea3a394ded58dd6ecca76260e08e"} {"question" "q-75317" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-75317" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3{x}_{i-1}^{2}+4{y}_{j-1}^{2}"] ["math" "4{x}_{i-1}^{2}+7{y}_{j-1}^{2}-12"] ["math" "4{x}_{i-1}^{2}+7{y}_{j}^{2}-12"] ["math" "4{x}_{i}^{2}+7{y}_{j}^{2}-12"] ["math" "5{x}_{i}^{2}+5{y}_{j}