ultivariable/14072378/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813289935f314fed96cd4ff74649733f6e26ea3a394ded58dd6ecca76260e08e"} {"question" "q-75328" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-75328" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "130-3{x}_{i-1}^{2}-5{y}_{j-1}^{2}"] ["math" "130-3{x}_{i-1}^{2}-5{y}_{j}^{2}"] ["math" "130-3{x}_{i}^{2}-5{y}_{j}^{2}"] ["math" "3{x}_{i-1}^{2}+4{y}_{j-1}^{2}"] ["math" "3{x}_{i}^{2}+4{y}_{j}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-75328" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "130-3{x}_{i}^{2}-5{y}_{j}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-123514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $R=[2,4]\\times [-4,-3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=7x-4y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-123514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=7x-4y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=7x-4y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/a44c2586978022663635d1f35399166c1ae32963fe0f4bffebd21966ad40bac5.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=7{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}_{(}f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(7{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $7{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-123514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813289935f314fed96cd4ff74649733f6e26ea3a394ded58dd6ecca76260e08e"} {"question" "q-123514" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-123514" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}_{i-1}+4{y}_{j}"] ["math" "2{x}_{i}+4{y}_{j-1}"] ["math" "7{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j}"] ["math" "7{x}_{i}-4{y}_{j-1}"] ["math" "7{x}_{i}-4{y}_{j}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-123514" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-123513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $R=[-1,1]\\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=5x-3y+20.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-123513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=5x-3y+20$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=5x-3y+20$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/a44c2586978022663635d1f35399166c1ae32963fe0f4bffebd21966ad40bac5.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}_{(}f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-123513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813289935f314fed96cd4ff74649733f6e26ea3a394ded58dd6ecca76260e08e"} {"question" "q-123513" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-123513" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j}"] ["math" "5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j-1}+20"] ["math" "5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20"] ["math" "5{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}+20"] ["math" "{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j-1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-123513" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-123518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $R=[-2,1]\\times [3,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=4y-5x-1.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-123518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=4y-5x-1$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=4y-5x-1$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/ffa57d3e7fed08212f12d4b9d7c2e0a4d33a3aac71c8b8a03d1a9a7364484deb.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/c4aa9e96fe72a8fb31ab62ff7eb0695cc64992bb9433be516461915a5c92baff.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})=4{y}_{j-1}-5{x}_{i}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(4{y}_{j-1}-5{x}_{i}-1)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $4{y}_{j-1}-5{x}_{i}-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-123518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813289935f314fed96cd4ff74649733f6e26ea3a394ded58dd6ecca76260e08e"} {"question" "q-123518" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-123518" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4{y}_{j-1}-5{x}_