72378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-75061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=5y-x+3$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=5y-x+3$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/ffa57d3e7fed08212f12d4b9d7c2e0a4d33a3aac71c8b8a03d1a9a7364484deb.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/c4aa9e96fe72a8fb31ab62ff7eb0695cc64992bb9433be516461915a5c92baff.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})=5{y}_{j-1}-{x}_{i}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{y}_{j-1}-{x}_{i}+3)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $5{y}_{j-1}-{x}_{i}+3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-75061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "813289935f314fed96cd4ff74649733f6e26ea3a394ded58dd6ecca76260e08e"} {"question" "q-75061" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-75061" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5{y}_{j-1}-{x}_{i-1}+3"] ["math" "5{y}_{j-1}-{x}_{i}+3"] ["math" "5{y}_{j}-{x}_{i-1}+3"] ["math" "5{y}_{j}-{x}_{i}+3"] ["math" "{y}_{j-1}-{x}_{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "q-75061" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5{y}_{j-1}-{x}_{i}+3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/state.json" "file_sha256" "779edcfc3ca8df7aa038d6461910be89ca65bfb416374d83a521fa981859e6c4"} {"question" "e-6247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $R = [0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x+2y.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/example-6247.json" "file_sha256" "3958c9bded0abb73144cbcbcb4cdea59d382bc7b7859dcf5c07c73f68d948ec1"} {"question" "e-6247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y$. This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})={x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/example-6247.json" "file_sha256" "3958c9bded0abb73144cbcbcb4cdea59d382bc7b7859dcf5c07c73f68d948ec1"} {"question" "e-6249" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $R = [0,1] \\times [2,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 10-x^2-y^2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/example-6249.json" "file_sha256" "97f2de1b086ff6dfc67920bb04c1c64d4bf95994d3e262fc5d0da2dbd5e64c25"} {"question" "e-6249" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) =10-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $x$ increases on $[0,1]$, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = 10-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[2,3].$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/4a10c8332a5f346d393c37531c13db6aa69d4cecb241efd7c34d57f32d5a98b8.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=10-{x}_{i}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(10-{x}_{i}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/example-6249.json" "file_sha256" "97f2de1b086ff6dfc67920bb04c1c64d4bf95994d3e262fc5d0da2dbd5e64c25"} {"question" "e-9496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $R = [2,3] \\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x - y + 3.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/example-9496.json" "file_sha256" "080a03e04483a3ff78253e65f3738b30fe698301e7f67c8ffa8b759f2ddade0b"} {"question" "e-9496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x - y + 3$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x - y + 3$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/assets/a44c2586978022663635d1f35399166c1ae32963fe0f4bffebd21966ad40bac5.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})={x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1 \\leq i \\leq m$ and $1 \\leq j \\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}_{(}f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}+3)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072378/example-9496.json" "file_sha256" "080a03e04483a3ff78253e65f3738b30fe698301e7f67c8ffa8b759f2ddade0b"}] "usage" {"e-9496" [] "q-75055" [] "e-6247" [] "e-6249" [] "q-75061" []} "basis" 2648 "retractions" [[17592186152635 :question/problem "Let $R = [1, 2] \\cdot [2, 3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x, y) = 4x^{2} + y^{2}$.\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R$, where\n\n$P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}, P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}, P = P_{1} \\cdot P_{2}$.\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n$L(f, P) = ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)AAAAAΔx_{i}Δy_{j}$\nwhere $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$ and $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$, what is the missing expression in the double summation above?"] [17592186152637 :question/problem "Let $R = [0, 1] \\cdot [0, 1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x, y) = 5y - x + 3$.\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R$, where\n\n$P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}, P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}, P = P_{1} \\cdot P_{2}$.\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n$L(f, P) = ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)AAAAAΔx_{i}Δy_{j}$\nwhere $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$ and $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$, what is the missing expression in the double summation above?"] [17592186151866 :question/problem "Let $R = [0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x+2y$. Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R$, where\n\n$P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}, P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}, P = P_{1} \\cdot P_{2}$.\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P)$."] [17592186151866 :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL(f, P) &= ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)m_{ij}Δx_{i}Δy_{j}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}$.\n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2615/Source/Images/87ff4da53aaa0d24860e1ce4c87670e6.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2615/Source/Images/ded242afabd5cfa40778881b586cae44.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y$. This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2615/Source/Images/c48db414a7ab06b8e9aee0c509f1a013.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm_{ij} &= f(x_{i - 1}, y_{j - 1}) = x_{i - 1} + 2y_{j - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all\n\n$$\n1\\leq i\\leq m\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n1\\leq j\\leq n\n$$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL(f, P) &= ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)(x_{i - 1} + 2y_{j - 1})Δx_{i}Δy_{j}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186151867 :question/problem "Let $R = [0,1] \\times [2,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 10-x^2-y^2$.\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R$, where\n\n$P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}, P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}, P = P_{1} \\cdot P_{2}$.\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P)$."] [17592186151867 :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL(f, P) &= ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)m_{ij}Δx_{i}Δy_{j}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}$.\n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2615/Source/Images/b4cb4b22e32666ef93b6b0cb8bdf196a.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) =10-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $x$ increases on $[0,1]$, and\n- $f(x,y) = 10-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[2,3]$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2615/Source/Images/c0d4216d9454a8c106a83aaca48b9e57.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y$. This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2615/Source/Images/3c7f764f4959d3fad12cd0df70d46b14.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm_{ij} &= f(x_{i}, y_{j}) = 10 - x_{i}^{2} - y_{j}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all\n\n$$\n1\\leq i\\leq m\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n1\\leq j\\leq n\n$$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL(f, P) &= ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)(10 - x_{i}^{2} - y_{j}^{2})Δx_{i}Δy_{j}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186151969 :question/problem "Let $R = [2,3] \\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x - y + 3$.\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R$, where\n$P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}, P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}, P = P_{1} \\cdot P_{2}$.\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P)$."] [17592186151969 :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL(f, P) &= ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)m_{ij}Δx_{i}Δy_{j}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}$.\n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2615/Source/Images/4707fec393fa97f6a2a8bd379ea8574b.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x - y + 3$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n- $f(x,y) = x - y + 3$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2615/Source/Images/7d6f2f08ee2c75640b099bc91d36aef8.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y$. This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2615/Source/Images/9e0e5cae4e2067faf6025f08cbbd6685.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm_{ij} &= f(x_{i - 1}, y_{j}) = x_{i - 1} - y_{j} + 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all\n\n$$\n1 \\leq i \\leq m\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n1 \\leq j \\leq n\n$$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL_{(}f, P) &= ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)(x_{i - 1} - y_{j} + 3)Δx_{i}Δy_{j}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186150721 17592186150722 17592186150723 17592186150724 17592186150725 17592186150733 17592186150734 17592186150735 17592186150736 17592186150737] "immutable_fields" [[17592186150720 :answer-field/correct] [17592186150720 :answer-field/id] [17592186150720 :answer-field/key] [17592186150720 :answer-field/type] [17592186150732 :answer-field/correct] [17592186150732 :answer-field/id] [17592186150732 :answer-field/key] [17592186150732 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
